---
import data from '../data/generated/spatial_robustness.json';

type CurvePoint = (typeof data.curves)[number]['values'][number];

const ols = data.curves.find((curve) => curve.estimator === 'OLS HC3')!;
const sem = data.curves.find((curve) => curve.estimator === 'SEM GMM')!;
const chart = { width: 900, height: 430, left: 78, right: 24, top: 30, bottom: 76 };
const plotWidth = chart.width - chart.left - chart.right;
const plotHeight = chart.height - chart.top - chart.bottom;
const allPoints = data.curves.flatMap((curve) => curve.values);
const xMin = Math.min(...allPoints.map((point) => point.imd_score));
const xMax = Math.max(...allPoints.map((point) => point.imd_score));
const yMin = 49.5;
const yMax = 53.5;
const xTicks = [2, 20, 40, 60, 69];
const yTicks = [50, 51, 52, 53];
const x = (value: number) => chart.left + ((value - xMin) / (xMax - xMin)) * plotWidth;
const y = (value: number) => chart.top + ((yMax - value) / (yMax - yMin)) * plotHeight;
const linePath = (points: CurvePoint[], key: 'prediction_pct' | 'ci_lower_pct' | 'ci_upper_pct') =>
	points.map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'}${x(point.imd_score).toFixed(2)},${y(point[key]).toFixed(2)}`).join(' ');
const ribbonPath = (points: CurvePoint[]) => {
	const upper = linePath(points, 'ci_upper_pct');
	const lower = [...points]
		.reverse()
		.map((point) => `L${x(point.imd_score).toFixed(2)},${y(point.ci_lower_pct).toFixed(2)}`)
		.join(' ');
	return `${upper} ${lower} Z`;
};
---

<section class="spatial-robustness" id="spatial-robustness" aria-labelledby="spatial-robustness-title">
	<header class="spatial-robustness-heading">
		<div>
			<p class="method-label">Spatial robustness</p>
			<h3 id="spatial-robustness-title">The deprivation gradient weakens when residual spatial dependence is modelled.</h3>
		</div>
		<p>
			The adjusted non-spatial model retains strongly clustered residuals. A heteroskedastic GMM spatial error model tests whether the IMD association remains after representing correlated, unobserved spatial structure.
		</p>
	</header>

	<div class="spatial-robustness-grid">
		<figure class="sem-comparison" aria-labelledby="sem-comparison-title">
			<header class="sem-chart-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="method-label">Conditional fast-food composition</p>
					<h4 id="sem-comparison-title">Non-spatial and Rook spatial-error estimates</h4>
				</div>
				<div class="sem-legend" aria-label="Chart legend">
					<span><i class="sem-key sem-key-ols"></i>OLS HC3</span>
					<span><i class="sem-key sem-key-rook"></i>Rook SEM</span>
				</div>
			</header>

			<div class="sem-chart-frame">
				<svg viewBox={`0 0 ${chart.width} ${chart.height}`} role="img" aria-labelledby="sem-svg-title sem-svg-desc">
					<title id="sem-svg-title">Adjusted fast-food share across IMD score under OLS and a Rook spatial error model</title>
					<desc id="sem-svg-desc">The OLS estimate rises by approximately 2.26 percentage points, while the spatial error estimate remains almost flat. Shaded ribbons show 95 percent confidence intervals.</desc>

					<g class="sem-grid">
						{yTicks.map((tick) => (
							<>
								<line x1={chart.left} x2={chart.width - chart.right} y1={y(tick)} y2={y(tick)} />
								<text x={chart.left - 14} y={y(tick) + 5} text-anchor="end">{tick.toFixed(0)}</text>
							</>
						))}
						{xTicks.map((tick) => (
							<>
								<line x1={x(tick)} x2={x(tick)} y1={chart.top} y2={chart.height - chart.bottom} />
								<text x={x(tick)} y={chart.height - chart.bottom + 27} text-anchor="middle">{tick}</text>
							</>
						))}
					</g>

					<path class="sem-ribbon sem-ribbon-ols" d={ribbonPath(ols.values)} />
					<path class="sem-ribbon sem-ribbon-rook" d={ribbonPath(sem.values)} />
					<path class="sem-line sem-line-ols" d={linePath(ols.values, 'prediction_pct')} />
					<path class="sem-line sem-line-rook" d={linePath(sem.values, 'prediction_pct')} />

					<line class="sem-axis" x1={chart.left} x2={chart.width - chart.right} y1={chart.height - chart.bottom} y2={chart.height - chart.bottom} />
					<line class="sem-axis" x1={chart.left} x2={chart.left} y1={chart.top} y2={chart.height - chart.bottom} />
					<text class="sem-axis-label" x={chart.left + plotWidth / 2} y={chart.height - 16} text-anchor="middle">IMD score · higher values indicate greater deprivation</text>
					<text class="sem-axis-label" transform={`translate(20 ${chart.top + plotHeight / 2}) rotate(-90)`} text-anchor="middle">Predicted fast-food share (%)</text>
				</svg>
			</div>

			<figcaption>
				Reference-profile predictions across the IMD-score 1st–99th percentile range. Shaded ribbons are pointwise 95% confidence intervals.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<aside class="sem-diagnostics" aria-label="Spatial model diagnostics">
			<article>
				<span>OLS residual Moran’s I</span>
				<strong>{data.baseline.residual_morans_i.toFixed(3)}</strong>
				<small>Strong residual geographic clustering</small>
			</article>
			<article>
				<span>Rook SEM λ</span>
				<strong>{data.rook_sem.lambda.toFixed(3)}</strong>
				<small>{data.rook_sem.undirected_edges.toLocaleString('en-GB')} shared-boundary links</small>
			</article>
			<article class="sem-contrast-card">
				<span>IMD 1st–99th percentile contrast</span>
				<strong><b>+{data.baseline.imd_change_percentage_points.toFixed(2)}</b><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><b>+{data.rook_sem.imd_change_percentage_points.toFixed(2)} pp</b></strong>
				<small>OLS HC3 → Rook SEM</small>
			</article>
			<p>Filtered-innovation Moran’s I is {data.rook_sem.filtered_residual_morans_i.toFixed(3)}: much smaller, but still outside the permutation reference range. The SEM reduces spatial dependence without fully whitening the residuals.</p>
		</aside>
	</div>

	<div class="network-sensitivity">
		<div>
			<p class="method-label">Alternative dependence structure</p>
			<h4>Delivery-network similarity provides a second spatial weights design.</h4>
		</div>
		<p>
			LSOAs are linked by the Jaccard similarity of their deliverable restaurant sets, using top-{data.network_sensitivity.top_k.join(', top-')} networks. These models also flatten the IMD contrast to {data.network_sensitivity.imd_change_range_percentage_points[0].toFixed(2)}–{data.network_sensitivity.imd_change_range_percentage_points[1].toFixed(2)} percentage points, but λ reaches {data.network_sensitivity.lambda_range[0].toFixed(2)}–{data.network_sensitivity.lambda_range[1].toFixed(2)} and prediction levels shift with network size. They are retained as exploratory sensitivity tests, not estimates of delivery spillovers.
		</p>
	</div>

	<p class="robustness-conclusion">
		<strong>Interpretation.</strong> The evidence supports strong spatial patterning in digital fast-food availability, but the independent deprivation gradient cannot yet be separated confidently from spatially structured market geography. This is specification sensitivity—not evidence that deprivation has no effect.
	</p>
</section>
